      "interpretation": "Decrease in concentration of individual and grouped parent PFAS (e.g., PFOA, PFOS, long-chain PFAS, 4:2 FTS, 6:2 FTS) between influent and effluent or across treatment time, expressed as degradation efficiency. This measures parent-compound loss and removal in the treated groundwater, which the authors interpret as PFAS destruction.",
      "reported_term": "PFAS degradation efficiency / PFAS destruction"
    },
    {
      "endpoint_type": "defluorination",
      "evidence_locator_ids": [
        "S07-E02",
        "S07-E06",
        "S07-E08"
      ],
      "interpretation": "Increase in aqueous fluoride concentration as PFAS concentrations and AOF decreased was used to infer that a portion of PFAS organic fluorine was mineralized to inorganic fluoride (defluorination).",
