      "interpretation": "The authors describe high-frequency ultrasound as mineralizing PFAS to fluoride and CO2 based on prior bench-scale work. In this field study, mineralization is inferred from partial conversion of AOF to fluoride, but complete carbon mineralization (e.g., CO2 measurement) was not reported in the provided text, so mineralization evidence is limited to fluorine-side mass balance rather than full carbon fate.",
      "reported_term": "PFAS mineralization"
    },
    {
      "endpoint_type": "other",
      "evidence_locator_ids": [
        "S07-E02",
        "S07-E06"
      ],
      "interpretation": "A simplified fluorine mass balance was conducted using three measures: (1) sum of fluorine in six PFAS with highest concentrations, (2) AOF, and (3) total fluoride. These were converted to moles of fluorine and compared between influent and effluent to estimate the fraction of PFAS-bound fluorine converted to fluoride and to evaluate creation of shorter-chain PFAS not otherwise quantified.",
      "reported_term": "Fluorine mass balance"
    }
